After the arrival of an investigational product in the national territory, the following documents must be presented:

*   A copy of the Special Communication (CE), Specific Special Communication (CEE), or the Document for Importation of Product(s) under investigation of the Clinical Development Dossier of Medication (DDCM) issued by the competent technical area of Anvisa at its headquarters [RDC 9/2015, Art. 74, I];
*   A copy of the document delegating importation responsibilities, in cases where the importation is performed by someone other than the DDCM holder [RDC 9/2015, Art. 74, II];
*   A term of responsibility for importation intended for clinical research, as provided in sanitary regulations for imported goods and products [RDC 9/2015, Art. 74, III];
*   A copy of the bill of lading [RDC 9/2015, Art. 74, IV]; and
*   A copy of the commercial invoice [RDC 9/2015, Art. 74, V].

Additionally, if there has been any change to the investigational products or their specifications previously informed in the CE, CEE, or DDCM import document, the updated document must be presented at the customs clearance location [RDC 9/2015, Art. 76].

