When filing for the registration of a new biological product, the applicant must submit the following documents in addition to the petition forms and proof of payment:

*   **Company and Technical Documentation:**
    *   Declaration of the company's size (economic capacity) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the Operating License and/or Sanitary Permit [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the Certificate of Authorization for Company Operation or its publication in the Official Gazette (DOU) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the updated Technical Responsibility Certificate issued by the Regional Pharmacy Council [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Technical justification for the product registration [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Technical report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Therapeutic experimentation report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Pharmacovigilance report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30].

*   **Manufacturing and Quality Documentation:**
    *   Copy of the Certificate of Good Manufacturing Practices (CBPF) issued by Anvisa for all manufacturers of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, primary packaging, finished product, diluent, and adjuvant [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the CBPF issued by the competent sanitary authority of the country where the manufacturer of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, primary packaging, finished product, diluent, and adjuvant is located [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the national, international, or internal company compendium specifying the finished biological product [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Additional information regarding TSE (Transmissible Spongiform Encephalopathy) control, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30].

*   **Regulatory and Product Information:**
    *   History of the product's registration status in other countries, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the registration proof in the country of origin issued by the competent sanitary authority [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Copy of the package insert model approved by the sanitary authority of the country of origin, with a sworn translation [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Models of the package insert and primary/secondary packaging [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Updated pharmacovigilance data, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
    *   Barcode (GTIN) or identification and security mechanisms for product tracking [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30].

*   **Clinical Studies:**
    *   Protocols and reports of clinical studies, including pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, and pivotal safety and efficacy studies [RDC 55/2010, Art. 46].

*   **Specific Requirements for Biotechnological Products:**
    *   Description of master and working cell banks [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
    *   Characterization of the active substance and its characterization in the finished biological product [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34].

