For the registration of biotechnological products, the requesting company must present the following information regarding master and working cell banks [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34]:

*   Description of the master and working cell banks used in the manufacturing of the biotechnological product [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Sequence of the cloned gene [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of the clone selection and expression control methods [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of the vector insertion method into the cell [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Documentation related to the genetic stability of the vector in the host cell [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of the host cell strain/lineage [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Determination of the maximum in vitro cell age [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of the expression vector used for the development of the master cell bank [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of the cell bank system, identifying the batch number of the master and working cell banks used for the production of clinical and industrial batches [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34];
*   Description of quality control and stability activities during the production and storage of the master and working cell banks [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34]; and
*   List and frequency of tests used to evaluate the stability of the master and working cell banks [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34].

